TTPS served on node1 port 8443\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e16d390a866a4230\",\"cmd-9387412e11e14455\",\"cmd-fbb1dff5e9ae4968\",\"cmd-5bb97a730fcd4ab6\"],\"summary\":\"nginx config validated, listening on 0.0.0.0:8443/[::]:8443, firewalld port opened, curl returns http_code=200 over TLS\"},{\"requirement\":\"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7fa528522ea74c8e\",\"cmd-0d239e5ca67d4a8b\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline cert serial/expiry captured at 10:01:27; cert-renew.timer fired and renew-cert.sh automatically issued a new cert (new serial, extended notAfter) at 10:04:39, logged in /var/log/renew-cert.log and confirmed via systemctl status of the oneshot service\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0d239e5ca67d4a8b\",\"cmd-d7f77e35d02f4f3c\"],\"summary\":\"Immediately after the automatic renewal, curl to :8443 still returned 200, and a live TLS handshake (openssl s_client) served the exact new certificate serial, proving nginx reloaded and picked up the rotated cert without downtime\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a95a2943d2474f8a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 83a0a80f-773c-4f3e-9137-1e7aa887b07a, nginx/cert-renew.timer active, HTTPS 200, live cert serial matching renewed cert\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and execution\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2251d467984f4d4a\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded `systemctl reboot` on node1 so the exec call returned before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity proving restart occurred\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cbb70143a7174e77\"],\"summary\":\"After polling through connection timeouts/resets while the node was down, exec succeeded again and boot_id changed to ee5486d2-7701-4036-a9ac-7525a4e03daf (new uptime since 10:05:10), proving an actual reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required services, 